    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3070\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the estates, powers and trusts law, in relation to\neliminating the 21-year limit for the duration of pet trusts\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nTo eliminate the 21 years limit for the duration of pet trusts.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection1. The section heading and subdivision (a) and (b) of section\n7-8.1 of the estates, powers and trusts law, as added by chapter 159\nof the laws of 1996, such section as renumbered by chapter 630 of the\nlaws of 2003 is amended to remove the 21 year maximum time period on\nthe pet trust.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nPassing this bill will allow for people to not have a set limit on how\nlong they can keep their pet under trusts. The laws of 1996 are\nproblematic for pet owners of animals other than dogs and cats.  Those\nlaws were created for those domestic animals with shorter life spans.\nAnimals such as horses with the average life span of 30 years and\ncertain species of birds are not protected for their full life\nexpectancy. Young pets and pets with long life expectancies tend to\noutlive the time period in which they are covered by the trust.\nAllowing pet trust to continue until no animal is covered under it\nwould be useful in order to ensure pet owners that even their young\nanimals will be covered for the full life after their death. Pet\nowners should have the option available to make these trusts last for\nthe lifetime of their pet.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
